# DS Bot mobile bridge provenance

The extracted `server/auth.js`, `server/projection.js` and transport in `server/server.js`
originate in this same Apache-2.0 licensed repository at commit
253407cf76062b2aa60bc5d039415aaa1c9867c4, under `ds-bot/src/mobile/`.
The transport is adapted to this independent entry and its restricted capabilities.
Candidate 0.0.5 composes this repository's reviewed group-bridge entry/adapter,
group projection and restricted actions-bridge module; those source directories
are read-only inputs to this candidate. The Apache-2.0 LICENSE is retained from
the bridge/group package lineage. Candidate fixture code copies the reviewed
npm DS Bot group candidate into its own ignored home and retains that package's
LICENSE; neither the patched fixture nor its test operator is in the tarball.
See the included LICENSE. The new entry and adapter are original work in this repository.

The repository's review-only candidate patch (not included in this release tarball)
targets the publicly published npm `ds-bot@0.1.7` package,
Apache-2.0, npm tarball integrity:
sha512-xRiXIpDfemkZ2l6lDwu7ZKSnn0a2c26BsZ7e+eEOkQ1AknXOKretK52Yuq1yfG6p4XCObmUiXR1tdGo7EQIStw==
The existing source fixture was downloaded to an ignored isolated directory;
this candidate reuses it by copying it into its own ignored test home.
It neither imports nor modifies a user's installed DS Bot or DSH files.

`ws@8.18.3` is a public MIT-licensed dependency; its license ships with that package.
`@deepseek-ai/schemastery@3.18.5` is a public MIT-licensed peer dependency.
Public DSH 0.2.0-rc.2 and 0.2.1-rc.2 dependencies are fixture-only and retain their own licenses.

